WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.972
U N J C versus U N C threads, and what changes on the internal thread.

2
00:00:09.583 --> 00:00:13.030
Here's a standard U N C external thread, cut

3
00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.771
in half so you can see both sides.

4
00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:19.247
Its root can be flat, with sharp corners. Under

5
00:00:19.347 --> 00:00:23.007
load, those corners are where fatigue cracks start.

6
00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.317
On U N J C, the root must be a

7
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:30.113
controlled radius, fifteen to eighteen hundredths of the pitch.

8
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:35.956
The rounded root sits higher, so the external minor diameter is larger.

9
00:00:36.056 --> 00:00:39.916
U N J C external threads are class three A only.

10
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.872
Now the mating part: a nut with a standard U N C internal thread.

11
00:00:45.966 --> 00:00:49.466
Zoom in on one root, at true proportions.

12
00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:53.922
Here's the bolt's rounded root, and the nut's crest

13
00:00:54.022 --> 00:00:56.707
at the standard U N C minor diameter.

14
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.065
The corners of the nut's crest run into the root radius. That's

15
00:01:01.165 --> 00:01:05.292
metal on metal, right where the bolt is most highly stressed.

16
00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:09.377
So U N J C internal threads have a larger minimum

17
00:01:09.477 --> 00:01:14.307
minor diameter. The crest moves out, and clears the radius.

18
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.535
Back to the full thread. Pitch diameter and major diameter

19
00:01:19.635 --> 00:01:22.412
are the same as U N C class three B.

20
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.068
Only the minor diameter changes. It's larger, so you drill or

21
00:01:27.168 --> 00:01:32.120
bore bigger, and you get about ten percent less thread engagement.

22
00:01:32.716 --> 00:01:35.452
To check it, use standard three B GO

23
00:01:35.552 --> 00:01:38.760
and NO GO thread plugs for pitch diameter.

24
00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:43.070
Then check the minor diameter separately, with a plain

25
00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.710
plug gauge to the U N J C limits.

26
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.133
Here are the minimum minor diameters for every standard U N

27
00:01:51.233 --> 00:01:54.820
C and U N J C internal thread, class three B.

28
00:01:58.916 --> 00:02:03.808
And the larger sizes. The U N J C minor is always bigger.

29
00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:11.976
Always confirm the exact limits on the print and

30
00:02:12.076 --> 00:02:14.064
in A S M E B 1 point 15.
